1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ingeborg er n. saman m Bjørn og Asbjørn i odelsmanntalet 1563. Ingeborg skatta for 1 v. korn. P. Valand meiner at dett var Ingeborg Toresdtr frå Berge i Forsand enkje etter Morten Bjørnson (Vikesdal 2.1)  i Egersun
2 CONC d 1521. Valand trur ho budde hjå sonen Bjørn her på Ivesdal i 1563.  Bjerkreimboka II (3) Gnr. 43 Ivesdal Page 1289.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingeborg is n. Together with Bjørn and Asbjørn in the cultivated men's speech in 1563. Ingeborg taxes for 1 v. Grain. P. Valand thinks that it was Ingeborg Toresdtr from Berge in Forsand, after Morten Bjørnson (Vikesdal 2.1) in Eg
2 CONC ersund in 1521. Valand Trur Ho invited Bjørn here at Ivesdal in 1563. Bjerkreimboka II (3) Gnr. 43 Ivesdal Page 1289.  This tells me that Ingeborg's husband Morten Bjørnson (Vikesdal 2.1)  had die in 1563. Ingeborg lived with her 
2 CONC son Bjørn in Ivesdal in 1563. Bjørn Mortensen Ivesdal died in 1603. His son Morton Bjørnson Fotland Ivesdal (5.2). His Son Torkel Mortensen Hovland born 1575 Est.  (8) Bjerkreimboka I (8) Gnr. 15  Hovland Page 438. 
2 CONT  Just a reminder all the names do not belong to this family, Most of my information comes from Bjerkreimboka I, II
2 CONT  and Bjerkreimboka No. III.
