1 OCCU sokneprest i Egersund, Sokneprest nevnt i 1587, Prest
1 TITL Sogneprest
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '' 'Petrus Valand has argued that the priest Ole Jonsen was the son of Jon Guttormsen Larsgård, this has in recent times been almost refuted. Or shown as very unlikely. '' '
2 CONT
2 CONT Parish priest in Egersund 1577-1594. Was deposed by judgment of the bishop and chapter 11.10.1594 for his "loose relics with a woman in Eggersund"
2 CONT
2 CONT 22.02.1580 The Stavanger chapter received an open letter from Mr. Oluf Jonsen with his wife and children that they will enjoy, use and keep in their lifetime the party with groves and meadows in the farm Årstad (which has added it
2 CONC  since time immemorial) that belongs to the chapter . If they promise to maintain the farm and follow the law in every way and pay the annual land debt to the principals of the chapter, the application is granted. Source page 23-2
2 CONC 4 in [http://www.nb.no/nbsok/nb/da2d4d1c1371f08b888e7b8b5b1ba502?index "Brandrud, Andreas - Stavanger Domkapitels Protokol: 1571-1630"]
2 CONT
2 CONT '' 'Source: Roald Undheim's notes p.36. Ætt & Heim 1964 p.115 '' '. "Son of Bishop of Stavanger Jon Guttormson and wife Anna Eriksdtr. Orm to Vatne, Stord. Married 1) with Helga Tollaksdtr. Årstad, Egersund, died before 1594. Stav
2 CONC anger Domkap.prot.s.176 mentions:" Anno 94, 11 octobris , bleff h: Joen Oluffsøn (skal være '' 'Oluf Joensøn' '') affsat aff sit kald for sit løsachtigt leffnet med en quinde vdj Eggersund, saa faderen belaa den ene oc sønnen den 
2 CONC anden syster. "In 1597 it is mentioned that "'' 'Mr. Oluf Jonsøn, prejudice spr. in "Eckundsund '" "Knut Lauritssøn sued Aasz with his quinde and both their daughters", for some time ago they should have agreed to give him their d
2 CONC aughter, Marite Knudsdtr, and had detained him without answer. But the father did not show up for the court, so we do not know if he married her. He must at least have been quite old. He was still alive in 1625, when his share in 
2 CONC Store Ege is mentioned (Tingboka p.268) =. it was not with Knud Åse father and son had been in 1594 " '' 'NOTE: The information about his origin above has recently been refuted' '' Original source pages 96 and 176 in [http://www.n
2 CONC b.no/nbsok/nb/da2d4d1c1371f08b888e7b8b5b1ba502?index "Brandrud, Andreas - Stavanger Domkapitels Protokol: 1571-1630"]
2 CONT
2 CONT The girl mentioned above is: [http://www.geni.com/people/Marite-se/6000000016322913022 Marite Knutsdatter Åse]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mentioned at Årstad 1602-1605, 1617 and 1620-1625
2 CONT
2 CONT '' 'Tingmøte Sokndal skipreide, 25-01-1618:' '' "Her Olluff Jonnsenn paa Aarstad y Eggersund kom herfor rettenn och skød sitt schodsmaall thill miennige bønnder och allmou, som her dag thillstede var, och bekom dett gaatt i alle m
2 CONC ader . "
2 CONT
2 CONT '' 'Tingmøte Eigersund skipreide, 28-01-1618:' '' "Framkomb Thallak Aarstad herfor rettenn och klagid att '' 'her Olluff ibm' ''. Nu y sommer forledenn thuinndegannger haffde skornne hanns noed i sønnder, som hannd sade . her Ollu
2 CONC f '' 'haffde optagenn enn jordfast stienn vdmed hanns agger reenn och denn inndueltt paa for / ne / Elluffs leigmaall, som hand beuise ville. Der emmod berette' '' her Olluff '' 'och klagett, att Enndre Aarstad haffde nu vdj somme
2 CONC r for ledenn slagenn hanns quinde thou slag med enn ryffue, som hannd ville beuisligt giørre. "
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole has twisted in his older days? And here it also appears that he was married as late as the summer of 1617
2 CONT
2 CONT Last mentioned '' 'Tingmøte Målstevne på Storegge i Voll skipreide, 20-04-1625' '': "... Sammeledis udj samme steffningh hid udj rätt alle loteyerne, nemblig '' 'h: Olle paa Aarstadt' '' som eyer with his children j søu, his previ
2 CONC ous quindis Hellie Tholleffs daughter's odell, Olle Eye with his two brothers j søu, Lasse Ege j søu odell, noch j søu kiøbt och j søu pant, Peder Thengsdall on behalf of his quindis and stepchildren his quindis hellmingh j søu, b
2 CONC ørnenis arff j sou, pant ij søu, {och} Jsack Thengs j sou och Erick Store Ege j søu, huilken som schulle verre bestemand offuer ald gaarden och raade byxellen. "
2 CONT
2 CONT The case concerns who is the owner of Store Ege. Lasse Tollaksen thinks he is the best man. And it is stated here that '' 'Herr' '' Ole På Årstad owns together with his children a share that his previous wife, Helga Tollaksdatter,
2 CONC  had in Store Ege, namely 1 sheep in Helga's share.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lasse Tollaksen Store Ege alone owns 3 sheep (1 share, 1 bought, 1 mortgage), Ole Endresen Own with his two brothers (Tollak Endresen and Asser Tollaksen) owns 1 sheep, Peder Njeldsen Tengesdal on his wife's (Guri Hoskuldsdatter w
2 CONC idow of Tollak Larsen Tengesdal (Store Ege)) and on behalf of the stepchildren own the wife's half 1 sheep, the children's inheritance 1 sheep and mortgage 2 (the mortgage of Halvor Hadland and Peder Lille Ege) sheep. Isak Olsen T
2 CONC engs and Erik Torgersen Store Ege also own without stating how much.
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional information that refutes that he is the son of Jon Guttormsen:
2 CONT
2 CONT In a letter from Norde Larsgard in Hovet in Hallingdal, Rønnaug Olavsdatter mentions that she is the granddaughter of Bishop Jon Guttormson, and Anna Eiriksdatter Orm. Derm
