2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Jon Knutsson Høyland was mentioned in the 1664 census.  That year he
2 CONT was listed as the operator of a farm valued at 5± pund grain (almost 2 laupar smør).  He sowed 6 tønner grain and had a herd consisting of 3 horses and 20 cattle.  His estate was probated on 22 May 1671. Alsvik says that his estat
2 CONC e was probate d in 1672.  He paid tax as a farm owner from abour 1645 till about 1655.  In 1661he was listed as the owner of 1 "laup" 1 "pund" at Høyland, 4 "pund smør" at Øvre Bjørheim, 15 1/2 "mark smør" at Fremre Sedberg, Årdal
2 CONC  and 1/2 "pund" 4 "merker smør " at Kalsem.
2 CONT They had a female servant in 1645.  Jon was a juror from 1661 to 1667.  He participated in assessing people's tax possibility in 1662.
2 CONT In connection with the subscription of soldiers Jon Høyland met in court in June 1658 to explain about his stepsons who had not met for subscription and who did neither meed in court.  Peder Thorson stayed with his grandfather (mo
2 CONC ther's father) , Peder Foss, during the subscription, and the other, Thore Thorson, was "et barn".  Peder was sentenced to pay 10 "mark sølv" to become free.  Otherwise he would have to leave the country.
